WEBVTT

00:00:00.550 --> 00:00:02.235
Lesson 10.4.

00:00:02.235 --> 00:00:06.795
Options income: covered calls, cash-secured puts, options vaults.

00:00:06.795 --> 00:00:09.273
By the end of this lesson, you'll be able

00:00:09.273 --> 00:00:12.045
to earn option premium on assets you'd hold or

00:00:12.045 --> 00:00:14.700
buy anyway, knowing exactly what you give up.

00:00:16.000 --> 00:00:17.290
Here's the plan.

00:00:17.290 --> 00:00:18.975
First, the key ideas.

00:00:18.975 --> 00:00:21.690
Then, a worked example, step by step.

00:00:21.690 --> 00:00:23.215
Then, your checklist.

00:00:23.215 --> 00:00:25.377
And finally, a three-question quiz.

00:00:26.677 --> 00:00:28.422
from you at a higher

00:00:28.422 --> 00:00:30.165
strike. You keep the premium,

00:00:30.165 --> 00:00:31.917
and your upside is capped

00:00:31.917 --> 00:00:33.882
at the strike. you the

00:00:33.882 --> 00:00:35.327
asset at a lower

00:00:35.327 --> 00:00:38.467
strike. You keep the premium. If price falls below

00:00:38.467 --> 00:00:40.077
the strike, you buy

00:00:40.077 --> 00:00:41.702
at the strike. called

00:00:41.702 --> 00:00:43.867
away → repeat. don't choose the strikes.

00:00:43.867 --> 00:00:46.227
First, Covered call: you hold the asset

00:00:46.227 --> 00:00:48.225
and sell someone the right to buy it.

00:00:48.225 --> 00:00:51.312
Next, Cash-secured put: you hold stablecoins and sell

00:00:51.312 --> 00:00:53.905
someone the right to sell. Then, the wheel:

00:00:53.905 --> 00:00:56.622
sell puts until assigned → hold the asset

00:00:56.622 --> 00:00:57.808
→ sell calls until. And

00:00:57.808 --> 00:00:59.937
finally, Options vaults automate this

00:00:59.937 --> 00:01:01.722
on-chain. They add contract risk and you.

00:01:03.022 --> 00:01:05.537
Let's work an example,

00:01:05.537 --> 00:01:07.202
step by

00:01:07.202 --> 00:01:09.807
step. ETH at 3,000. about

00:01:09.807 --> 00:01:13.212
20.9% annualised if repeated at

00:01:13.212 --> 00:01:16.117
that premium, which it won't

00:01:16.117 --> 00:01:19.062
be exactly. Max gain for

00:01:19.062 --> 00:01:23.247
the week 10.4%. Break-even 2,988. the calculator

00:01:23.247 --> 00:01:27.787
to 0.44% on the cash for the week.

00:01:27.787 --> 00:01:31.892
If assigned, effective entry $2,688. Covered

00:01:31.892 --> 00:01:34.837
call: sell a 7-day 3,300 call

00:01:34.837 --> 00:01:39.499
for 0.4% ($12). Cash-secured put: sell a 7-day

00:01:39.499 --> 00:01:43.367
2,700 put for $12 with $2,700 reserved.

00:01:44.667 --> 00:01:47.301
Covered call: upside above the strike, plus

00:01:47.301 --> 00:01:49.457
the full downside of the asset.

00:01:49.457 --> 00:01:51.962
Cash-secured put: a crash through the strike.

00:01:53.262 --> 00:01:54.722
Here's your checklist.

00:01:54.722 --> 00:01:56.257
Do it now, for real.

00:01:56.257 --> 00:01:58.716
First, only on assets I'd hold (calls)

00:01:58.716 --> 00:02:00.782
or buy at the strike (puts).

00:02:00.782 --> 00:02:04.247
Next, Strike chosen from levels, not from the premium.

00:02:04.247 --> 00:02:08.782
Then, Annualised premium treated as "if repeated", never promised.

00:02:08.782 --> 00:02:11.867
And finally, Vault due diligence done if automating.

00:02:13.167 --> 00:02:14.377
Question 1.

00:02:14.377 --> 00:02:15.336
What do you give up

00:02:15.336 --> 00:02:16.582
by selling a covered call?

00:02:21.002 --> 00:02:23.887
The answer: Gains above the strike for that period.

00:02:25.187 --> 00:02:26.432
Question 2.

00:02:26.432 --> 00:02:30.342
Put strike 2,700, premium $15.

00:02:30.342 --> 00:02:31.912
Effective entry if assigned?

00:02:36.332 --> 00:02:39.447
The answer: $2,685.

00:02:40.747 --> 00:02:42.017
Question 3.

00:02:42.017 --> 00:02:43.932
Does premium protect you in a crash?

00:02:48.352 --> 00:02:51.317
The answer: Only by the size of the premium.

00:02:51.317 --> 00:02:53.102
The asset's downside remains.

00:02:54.402 --> 00:02:55.647
Let's recap.

00:02:55.647 --> 00:02:57.650
Covered call: you hold the asset and

00:02:57.650 --> 00:02:59.737
sell someone the right to buy it.

00:02:59.737 --> 00:03:02.212
Cash-secured put: you hold stablecoins and

00:03:02.212 --> 00:03:04.297
sell someone the right to sell.

00:03:04.297 --> 00:03:06.738
The wheel: sell puts until assigned →

00:03:06.738 --> 00:03:09.222
hold the asset → sell calls until.

00:03:09.222 --> 00:03:11.282
Options vaults automate this on-chain.

00:03:12.582 --> 00:03:15.097
Do the checklist now, before you move on.

00:03:15.097 --> 00:03:20.022
Next up, Lesson 10.5: Active concentrated-liquidity management.
